      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the railroad was routed through the county in 1882, Fordyce built a station three miles north after Toledo rejected the line, sparking Rison's birth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rison%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first home in the area was built in 1880 by lawyer and farmer James McMurtrey, long before the town was officially incorporated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rison%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Two Rison service stations, the Cities Service and Texaco, are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
